# Issue #699: generic OIDC RP layer (discovery, JWKS, id_token validation, PKCE)
# 1.6.9 patches CVE-2026-27962 (JWK header injection), CVE-2025-59420 (crit
# header authz bypass) and GHSA-pq5p-34cr-23v9 (JOSE DoS). See PR #700.
# 1.9.1 is the first release that patches all nine advisories open against
# 1.6.12, including GHSA-6v38-4h7w-rj9h (critical, empty JWS signatures),
# GHSA-7vr2-2fgp-9w7p, GHSA-8m4g-j4wp-wgcg and GHSA-c73q-w75p-j82v (high).
# 1.9.2 to 1.9.5 are security-only releases; 1.9.5 completes the fix for HMAC
# verification with a public key in authlib.jose (GHSA-f7j6-p4qx-gq99), the
# one Authlib module this backend imports (oidc.py).
# From 1.7 Authlib depends on joserfc and marks authlib.jose deprecated; it
# stays supported until Authlib 2.0. tests/test_oidc_token_validation.py pins
# the accept/reject behaviour this backend relies on across upgrades.
Authlib==1.9.5
